la is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-3,-1),$ and passes through the point $(-5,1).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-3,-1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+3=p{t}^{2},\\,y+1=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,1),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=1$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 2=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+3=(-\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y+1=2(-\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-t.\n$$" 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310421 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310422 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310423 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310424 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310425 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1041 "selection" 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310421 13194139534791 true] [17592186310420 1110 #uuid "88f24eaa-bd31-5c6c-80a0-5608034660ab" 13194139534791 true] [17592186310421 1034 "x+3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-t" 13194139534791 true] [17592186310421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534791 true] [17592186310421 1111 #uuid "f5cfbb25-241e-55fa-a7d4-89ae164d5aaf" 13194139534791 true] [17592186310422 1034 "x-3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}